<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>DW - English for Africa</title><subtitle type="html">News, Analysis and Service from Germany and Europe - in 30 Languages</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:44:39Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="/atoms/rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12756?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Guinea-Bissau votes to reshape presidency</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d002ee141fbbd33c851673167d43c51c6ce22bfe6bfb5b614acd91485dffe26</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:44:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T12:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.dw.com/en/guinea-bissau-votes-to-reshape-presidency/a-78562523--3df5be399db5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/guinea-bissau-votes-to-reshape-presidency/a-78562523?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The West African nation's military government wants to amend the constitution to give more powers to the president. The junta, which seized power last year, says it will hold elections in December.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Turkish, Somali forces free vessel seized by pirates in Somalia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:61b4f11023802ef7ceeac55c5883cee844da07fc0cb924038e37ad88162983dc</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:44:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T20:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.dw.com/en/turkish-somali-forces-free-vessel-seized-by-pirates-in-somalia/a-78560087--de7714620edd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkish-somali-forces-free-vessel-seized-by-pirates-in-somalia/a-78560087?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Turkish and Somali forces have freed the MV LUTUF after pirates hijacked the vessel off the coast of Somalia. The 10-day operation killed 14 alleged pirates and destroyed four boats used by the attackers.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Zimbabwe crash involving church minibus kills 27</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2a9b545a5ff9762d6be1b1973d4efc0fc7b9c77ec6a3ba4390482fcc2ce22b97</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:44:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T17:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.dw.com/en/zimbabwe-crash-involving-church-minibus-kills-27/a-78558710--108e8ca003fd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/zimbabwe-crash-involving-church-minibus-kills-27/a-78558710?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Dozens of people were killed when a minibus carrying churchgoers collided head-on with a truck in central Zimbabwe. The crash near the town of Chivhu is the latest deadly road accident in the African country.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Niger's defense ministry says soldiers attempted mutiny</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1915ea29ac477806b574591b7868e0d14d2cd41de5fbf26be1021a68bf3bb4f3</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:44:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T12:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.dw.com/en/niger-s-defense-ministry-says-soldiers-attempted-mutiny/a-78554001--b293ea6a9b27.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/niger-s-defense-ministry-says-soldiers-attempted-mutiny/a-78554001?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Dozens of rebeling soldiers were killed or arrested, state media said. The attack posed the latest threat to Niger's military junta, led by Abdourahamane Tchiani, who seized power in a 2023 coup.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Africa's aging autocrats fight to stay in power</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c02fe06a7e0a5c5bd31a8c1a157766ed31ace95496181efffe295a36ca4979d</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:44:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T14:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.dw.com/en/africa-s-aging-autocrats-fight-to-stay-in-power/a-78487210--45be184aa17e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/africa-s-aging-autocrats-fight-to-stay-in-power/a-78487210?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As some of Africa's longest-serving leaders grow older, they are using different tactics to extend their rule. But age, succession battles and public pressure pose new challenges.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>What does Saxony-Anhalt's election mean for migrants?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1b10edc53fbf792b79a0e5e72e3f37f203a5f5826eba95706072f308b80173fe</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:44:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T12:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.dw.com/en/what-does-saxony-anhalt-s-election-mean-for-migrants/a-78504553--ae71d2d9cd41.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-does-saxony-anhalt-s-election-mean-for-migrants/a-78504553?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The AfD could make history in the German state of Saxony-Anhalt. For many people with a migration background, the September 6 state election raises questions about belonging, security and their future in Germany.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>The great lake divide: Collapse vs. comeback</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4caef914e491e49a7330b4d914b08957681a9aee09a94c9d738b04102bac8d41</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:44:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T09:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.dw.com/en/the-great-lake-divide-collapse-vs-comeback/a-78460263--c86da47943ed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-great-lake-divide-collapse-vs-comeback/a-78460263?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As some of the world’s biggest lakes are vanishing in real time, others are proving that recovery is still within reach.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>40 years after the Lake Nyos disaster in Cameroon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e6a2fc28af1cc4795c4ab928774f4b553ff6903cba856762c8fdab827604096b</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:44:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-21T14:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.dw.com/en/40-years-after-the-lake-nyos-disaster-in-cameroon/a-78459694--fd23a1f9d902.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/40-years-after-the-lake-nyos-disaster-in-cameroon/a-78459694?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">On August 21, 1986, a silent cloud of carbon dioxide swept through villages around Lake Nyos in Cameroon, killing nearly 2,000 people in their sleep. Four decades later, survivors are still living with the trauma.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Amanal Petros: From refugee to European champion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0f6538eb7b83854331338a9752adad5869883d6921e2dc07dc39f80c517ef46b</id><updated>2026-08-30T14:44:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-19T11:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="/pages/www.dw.com/en/amanal-petros-from-refugee-to-european-champion/a-78428504--a9305ea94714.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/amanal-petros-from-refugee-to-european-champion/a-78428504?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Amanal Petros fled the Eritrean–Ethiopian war and came to Germany as a teenager. Now one of the world's top marathon runners, he recently won gold at the European Athletics Championships.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry></feed>
